When a page leaves full screen because another tab became current,
Ladybird tells the tab that held full screen, not the one that’s
current by then. Chromium does the same: When a tab is deactivated,
its FullscreenController::ExitExclusiveAccessIfNecessary() runs
NotifyTabExclusiveAccessLost(), which calls ExitFullscreen() on the
WebContents holding exclusive access rather than on the active one.
